index 0000000..4a2f4d8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/adr/0001-case-resolution-comments.md
@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+# ADR 0001: Record case resolutions as customer-visible comments
+
+## Status
+
+Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+Closing a support case requires a short resolution that the customer can read. Existing case comments already carry an author, timestamp, body, and internal/customer-visible flag.
+
+## Decision
+
+Store the trimmed resolution as a non-internal case comment authored by the user who closes the case. Persist the comment and the `CLOSED` status in one transaction; do not add a separate resolution field to the case.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Customers see how their case was resolved through the existing comment model, and the resolution retains normal comment authorship and ordering. A close operation is atomic and cannot leave a status without its resolution comment.
